Inter-VLAN routing within Location A is working correctly. From the affected VLAN 10 host (PC4, 172.16.10.4) we can reach the VLAN 20 host (Laptop0, 172.16.20.10) with 0% loss, and the reverse direction also succeeds. The TTL of 63 on both paths indicates a single routed hop, consistent with routing via router0.

