Root cause: No misconfiguration found. The reported outage was likely transient (e.g., initial ARP resolution or a brief port/VLAN transition) or a user-side test issue.

Corrective fix: No changes required. If the issue recurs intermittently, capture timestamps of failures and verify mswitch1’s trunk allow-list and STP state on the router0 uplink; otherwise, the network is healthy. 
